# Mobile — pending content shows a spinner, not an empty state

When a component can render before its data has arrived, **show a loading spinner** until the
load settles. Only then show the real content or a true empty state.

## Why

An empty message ("No description", "No episodes") while a request is still in flight is a lie.
The user sees a flash of "nothing here" and then the real data.

## Do

- Treat "not loaded yet" as a third state, distinct from empty and error.
- Gate empty copy on the load having **settled** (`isInitialLoading === false`, channel DTO
  arrived or the first fetch failed, etc.).
- Use the shared chrome: `LoadingSection`, `ListLoading`, `AuthAwareLoadState`, or
  `PodcastSectionList` `isInitialLoading`.
- Keep the spinner up through the first paint of a chip or tab whose body depends on a DTO that
  has not arrived yet (podcast About while the channel request is still out; Home media type
  while preferences resolve).

## Don't

- Don't render `ListEmpty` / "no summary" / "no items" while the request that would fill the
  body is still outstanding.
- Don't infer emptiness from `null` or `[]` when those also mean "not fetched yet".
- Don't skip the spinner because the data "usually arrives fast" or "comes with a parent
  payload" — the parent payload can still be pending.

